## Design

Priority: fun → easy → clear → selective → respectful. Fun is consequence and rhythm, not decoration.

- Dark, matte, editorial, layered. No neon-terminal chrome. No casino glow.
- Tokens only: `frontend/src/styles/tokens.css`, `product-hierarchy.css`, `product-rhythm.css`, `fantasy-phone.css`.
- Blue (`--experience-blue` / `--accent`) = current context and the next action. Nothing else.
- Teal = healthy/saved. Amber = attention. Red = destructive/blocking, plus the live auction clock under 5s. Gold = awards only — never the live high-bid figure.
- Hierarchy from surface, type, and spacing — not a border on every box. Token insets and gutters; text is never flush to a line and never smaller than `--text-xs` (12px computed).
- Editorial pages use one hero stack: `HubExperienceHero` + `HubExperienceLayout` + `HubExperienceSummary` from `HubUILayout.jsx`. Strategy is the board-first exception — no hero band.
- **Fix the primitive, not the page.** Shared CSS/components first. Measurable layout rules: `.cursor/rules/frontend-craft.mdc`.
- League-strip option menus paint above the Fantasy page below the strip. Raise `.hub-league-context-bar` (or portal the menu) — a later `.hub-page` at the same z-index covers overflowing menus.
- Copy lives in `*Presentation.js`. State the decision and the cost of getting it wrong. No slogan that could sit on another app. No “Submit”, no “You do not have permission” (use “Commissioner managed”).

## Product rules you may not bypass

- League policy changes apply to **new contracts only**. Say that once, next to Save.
- Rules Save writes the league on the form, not hub focus. Do not apply a late save that belongs to another league.
- Opening a Fantasy page does not change the saved league. Practice rooms never become strip focus. Only Switch league, or joining/creating a live league, writes focus.
- Switching Projections, Fantasy, or Tools returns you to the last destination you used in that area. Tapping the already-selected top-level tab reopens that area’s destination picker on phone.
- Applying a league template confirms, names what changes, and fills the form. It does not save. Offer undo until the next edit.
- Players-tab adds follow the acquisition calendar (`acquisitionWindow.js`). Staff Roster management may override; Players-tab adds may not.
- Do not invent a parallel rules or contract model. Merge/validate via `rulesPresentation.js`. Backend is authoritative.
- Fantasy lists people by **owner name**. Team nicknames may sit underneath or after a middot.
- One `<main id="main-content">` plus a skip link; do not nest a second main.
- Practice mock rooms have no Drop or Trade. Simulate uses live-bot pricing, shows N of the remaining pool, and never disables Discard. Never say Available players.
- Cap, Rosters, My team, and after-draft Roster management leftover is auction leftover: expiring 1-year keepers and Yrs-0 expirees are not committed. Against-cap is salary plus dead cap. After draft, staff Drop, Cut, and field edits write immediately. Owners Cut on My team after draft. Dead cap hits only the cut season. Dead cap floors to the lower dollar ($1 → $0, $7 → $3 at 50%).
- One-year expirees that cannot extend use Expiring — never Expires — FA. They enter the draft pool; undrafted names become free agents after the draft.
- Contract types shown to users are Rookie deal, Vet deal, and Extension — never Rookie Extension or Veteran Deal. Rookie deals and vet deals stay flat for the first term; the step-up starts on an Extension. Rules shows Keep vet deals flat and Allow vet deal extensions as their own toggles. Final-year rookie deals and vet deals may take one extension when their Rules toggle is on.
- A nomination queue stays on that manager's board only. Do not put another team's queue on room state.

